Ask statvfs whether a filesystem is local, on zedBSD

is_local_impl falls through to masking the statvfs flags with MNT_LOCAL.
MNT_LOCAL belongs to struct statfs and the mount interface; the field being
masked is struct statvfs's f_flag, which carries ST_ values.  On a system
that reaches this branch with a real statvfs, the two do not meet: the
constant is not declared by any header this file includes, and it would not
mean anything in that field if it were.

zedBSD reports ST_LOCAL in f_flag, which is the same question asked in the
terms that field is written in.

--- a/llvm/lib/Support/Unix/Path.inc
+++ b/llvm/lib/Support/Unix/Path.inc
@@ -570,6 +570,8 @@
   // The file system can have an arbitrary structure on z/OS; must go with the
   // conservative answer.
   return false;
+#elif defined(__ZEDBSD__)
+  return !!(STATVFS_F_FLAG(Vfs) & ST_LOCAL);
 #else
   return !!(STATVFS_F_FLAG(Vfs) & MNT_LOCAL);
 #endif
